    "ssml": "<speak xmlns:mstts=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xml:lang=\"en-US\"><voice name=\"en-US-Harper:MAI-Voice-2.1\"><mstts:express-as style=\"audiobook\"><prosody rate=\"-12%\"><p>It is Saturday. Maya is nine years old, and her brother Tom is six. Together they go to a flea market. In the corner stands an old table, and on the table there is a wooden radio. It has gold knobs and colourful buttons. When Maya comes closer, the radio suddenly hums quietly: Ding! A golden inscription appears on the radio: “For Maya and Tom.” The children open their eyes wide.</p></prosody></mstts:express-as></voice></speak>"
